// User Core profile — the base layer every user profile.jsonc is resolved
// over (ADR 0036, ADR 0057). Lists concat+dedupe with the user profile;
// scalars user-wins. A user drops something declared here via
// `programs_exclude`.
//
// `shell` is /bin/zsh: the entire tracked shell payload is zsh while
// .bashrc/.bash_profile/.profile are untracked — so a bash default landed a
// fresh install in a shell whose stowed config never loaded. The zsh package
// itself is NOT declared: ensure_login_shell_installed pacman-installs a
// user's login shell when the binary is missing. Root stays /bin/bash
// (ADR 0054, options.root_shell).
//
// `programs` is the standard tooling every real user gets: `zsh` (the
// interactive shell tooling + pre-warmed zinit cache + palette theme the stowed
// config expects — the login shell itself is the `shell` key above), plus
// `kitty` (the fleet terminal's seeded + stowable config + FiraCode Nerd font,
// ADR 0130 — the kitty binary itself is core/preset-owned), plus `lazygit` and
// `yazi` (seeded + stowable configs that own their package and follow the
// palette via ANSI-16, ADR 0132), plus
// `virt-manager`, plus `searxng` and its `podman` backend (podman precedes
// searxng — a required program must resolve earlier in the same user's list,
// ADR 0065), plus `pi` (the pi coding agent, served fleet-wide, ADR 0127).
// `docker` is NOT here — it is aquastias-specific (users/aquastias). The two VM
// test users exclude these — they exercise the system install path, not user
// programs.
{
  "shell": "/bin/zsh",
  "sudo": false,
  "groups": ["audio", "video", "storage", "optical", "network", "seat"],
  "programs": [
    "zsh", "kitty", "lazygit", "yazi", "virt-manager", "podman", "searxng",
    "pi", "claude", "nvim"
  ],
  "ssh_authorized_keys": []
}
